        JourneyDay(journeyID: "proverbs31", dayNumber: 15, title: "Clothed in Scarlet", scripture: "When it snows, she has no fear for her household; for all of them are clothed in scarlet.", scriptureReference: "Proverbs 31:21", reflection: "She's not anxious about the future because she's prepared in the present. 'Clothed in scarlet' means her family is well-provided for. Preparedness isn't worry — it's wisdom. She trusts God AND she does her part.", prompt: "Are you preparing wisely for challenges, or are you anxiously worrying about them? What's the difference?", actionStep: "Take one proactive step today to prepare for something you've been anxious about — then release the anxiety to God.", prayer: "Lord, replace my anxiety with wise preparation. Help me trust You while faithfully doing my part. Amen."),
        JourneyDay(journeyID: "proverbs31", dayNumber: 16, title: "Creating Beauty", scripture: "She makes coverings for her bed; she is clothed in fine linen and purple.", scriptureReference: "Proverbs 31:22", reflection: "She creates beauty in her environment and in herself — not out of vanity, but out of worship. Creating beauty is an act of reflecting God's character. Your home, your appearance, your spaces — they can all glorify Him.", prompt: "Where can you create beauty in your life today — in your home, your appearance, your relationships?", actionStep: "Beautify one space today — arrange flowers, light a candle, make your bed with intention. Let it be worship.", prayer: "Creator, help me reflect Your beauty in my environment and in my life. Let me create spaces that honor You. Amen."),
        JourneyDay(journeyID: "proverbs31", dayNumber: 17, title: "Her Influence", scripture: "Her husband is respected at the city gate, where he takes his seat among the elders of the land.", scriptureReference: "Proverbs 31:23", reflection: "Her influence isn't loud — it's deep. The people around her rise because of the atmosphere she creates. Your quiet faithfulness, your prayer, your encouragement — these shape the people closest to you.", prompt: "How does your faithfulness influence the people around you? Where can you be a greater source of strength?", actionStep: "Encourage someone in your circle today with a specific, genuine affirmation of who they're becoming.", prayer: "Lord, let my influence be deep and life-giving. Use my faithfulness to help others rise. Amen."),
        JourneyDay(journeyID: "proverbs31", dayNumber: 18, title: "Entrepreneurial Spirit", scripture: "She makes linen garments and sells them, and supplies the merchants with sashes.", scriptureReference: "Proverbs 31:24", reflection: "She creates, she produces, she sells. She has an entrepreneurial spirit — using her gifts to serve and provide. Whether you work in a home, an office, or a marketplace, your work has kingdom value.", prompt: "How are you using your skills and gifts to create value? Where might God be calling you to step out?", actionStep: "Use one of your skills to serve someone or create something of value today.", prayer: "Father, give me the courage and creativity to use my gifts boldly. Every skill You gave me has kingdom purpose. Amen."),
        JourneyDay(journeyID: "proverbs31", dayNumber: 19, title: "Clothed in Strength and Dignity", scripture: "She is clothed with strength and dignity.", scriptureReference: "Proverbs 31:25a", reflection: "Strength and dignity aren't things you earn — they're garments you put on by faith. They come from knowing Whose you are, not from what you achieve. When you walk in God's strength and the dignity He gives, you carry yourself differently.", prompt: "Do you see yourself as a woman of strength and dignity? What would change if you truly believed it?", actionStep: "Walk into every room today as though you're wearing strength and dignity — because you are.", prayer: "Lord, clothe me in Your strength and dignity today. Not the world's version, but Yours — unshakeable and grace-filled. Amen."),
        JourneyDay(journeyID: "proverbs31", dayNumber: 20, title: "Laughing at the Days to Come", scripture: "She can laugh at the days to come.", scriptureReference: "Proverbs 31:25b", reflection: "She laughs at the future — not because she's naive, but because she trusts the God who holds it. This is the ultimate freedom from anxiety. When you know Who holds tomorrow, you can face it with joy instead of fear.", prompt: "Can you laugh at the days to come? What fears about the future do you need to release to God?", actionStep: "Write down your biggest fear about the future. Then write underneath it: 'God holds this. I can laugh.'", prayer: "Father, I release my fears about the future into Your hands. Give me the faith to laugh at the days to come, trusting You completely. Amen."),
        JourneyDay(journeyID: "proverbs31", dayNumber: 21, title: "Wisdom on Her Tongue", scripture: "She speaks with wisdom.", scriptureReference: "Proverbs 31:26a", reflection: "Wise speech isn't about always having the right answer. It's about knowing when to speak, what to say, and how to say it. Wisdom on her tongue means her words are measured, intentional, and life-giving.", prompt: "Are your words wise? Do you speak with intention, or do you react without thinking?", actionStep: "Before every significant conversation today, pause and ask: 'What is the wise thing to say here?'", prayer: "Lord, put wisdom on my tongue. Help me speak with intention, not impulse. Let my words build up. Amen."),
        JourneyDay(journeyID: "proverbs31", dayNumber: 22, title: "Faithful Instruction", scripture: "Faithful instruction is on her tongue.", scriptureReference: "Proverbs 31:26b", reflection: "Her teaching isn't harsh or demanding — it's faithful and kind. Whether you're mentoring, parenting, leading, or simply sharing life with others, your instruction should be marked by both truth and tenderness.", prompt: "Who are you teaching or mentoring? Is your instruction marked by faithfulness and kindness?", actionStep: "Teach someone something today — a life lesson, a scripture, a skill — with gentleness and love.", prayer: "Lord, make me a faithful instructor. Let my words teach, guide, and encourage with Your kindness. Amen."),
        JourneyDay(journeyID: "proverbs31", dayNumber: 23, title: "Watching Over Her Household", scripture: "She watches over the affairs of her household.", scriptureReference: "Proverbs 31:27a", reflection: "Watching over isn't controlling — it's stewarding. She pays attention to the spiritual, emotional, and physical climate of her home. She notices what needs tending and tends it with care.", prompt: "What in your household or sphere of influence needs your attentive care right now?", actionStep: "Identify one area in your home or life that needs tending. Give it focused attention today.", prayer: "Lord, help me be a faithful watchwoman over my household — attentive, caring, and wise. Amen."),
        JourneyDay(journeyID: "proverbs31", dayNumber: 24, title: "No Bread of Idleness", scripture: "She does not eat the bread of idleness.", scriptureReference: "Proverbs 31:27b", reflection: "This isn't about hustle culture. It's about intentional living. She doesn't waste her days on things that don't matter. She's purposeful with her time — not busy, but fruitful. There's a difference.", prompt: "Where are you eating the 'bread of idleness' — wasting time on distractions instead of what matters?", actionStep: "Replace 30 minutes of a time-wasting habit with something purposeful today.", prayer: "Father, help me live intentionally — not busy, but fruitful. Redeem my time for Your purposes. Amen."),
        JourneyDay(journeyID: "proverbs31", dayNumber: 25, title: "Her Children Call Her Blessed", scripture: "Her children arise and call her blessed.", scriptureReference: "Proverbs 31:28a", reflection: "Legacy isn't built in a single moment — it's built in thousands of small, faithful ones. Whether you have children or not, your legacy is the lives you touch, the love you give, and the truth you live.", prompt: "What legacy are you building? What will the people closest to you say about your life?", actionStep: "Do one thing today that builds your legacy — an act of love that will be remembered.", prayer: "Lord, help me build a legacy of faithfulness. May the people I love call me blessed — not because I was perfect, but because I pointed them to You. Amen."),
        JourneyDay(journeyID: "proverbs31", dayNumber: 26, title: "Her Husband Praises Her", scripture: "Her husband also, and he praises her.", scriptureReference: "Proverbs 31:28b", reflection: "The people closest to you see you most clearly — your strengths and your struggles. When they praise you, it's because your character is consistent behind closed doors. Integrity is who you are when no one is watching.", prompt: "Are you the same person publicly and privately? Where do you need more integrity?", actionStep: "Choose consistency today — let your private life match your public character.", prayer: "Lord, make me consistent. Let my integrity behind closed doors match the person the world sees. Amen."),
        JourneyDay(journeyID: "proverbs31", dayNumber: 27, title: "Many Women Do Noble Things", scripture: "Many women do noble things, but you surpass them all.", scriptureReference: "Proverbs 31:29", reflection: "This isn't a ranking — it's a celebration. Every woman who walks in faith does noble things. But the specific way God has wired you? Irreplaceable. Don't compare your nobility to hers. Both are beautiful.", prompt: "What 'noble things' has God called you specifically to do? Can you celebrate them without comparison?", actionStep: "Celebrate one noble thing about yourself AND one noble thing about another woman today.", prayer: "Father, help me see the nobility in my calling without comparing it to anyone else's. We all do noble things by Your grace. Amen."),
        JourneyDay(journeyID: "proverbs31", dayNumber: 28, title: "Beyond Charm and Beauty", scripture: "Charm is deceptive, and beauty is fleeting.", scriptureReference: "Proverbs 31:30a", reflection: "The world chases charm and beauty — both of which fade. Charm can manipulate. Beauty fades with time. But what remains? Character. Integrity. A heart that fears the Lord. Build what lasts.", prompt: "Are you investing more in what fades or what lasts? Where is the imbalance?", actionStep: "Invest time today in your inner life — prayer, Scripture, character — instead of external appearance.", prayer: "Lord, help me invest in what lasts. Build my character, deepen my faith, and grow my love — things that never fade. Amen."),
        JourneyDay(journeyID: "proverbs31", dayNumber: 29, title: "A Woman Who Fears the Lord", scripture: "But a woman who fears the Lord is to be praised.", scriptureReference: "Proverbs 31:30b", reflection: "This is the heart of it all. Every noble quality of the Proverbs 31 woman flows from one source: she fears the Lord. Not cowering fear — reverent, awe-filled, loving devotion. When your life is built on this foundation, everything else falls into place.", prompt: "Is the fear of the Lord truly the foundation of your life? What would change if it were?", actionStep: "Spend 10 minutes in silence and awe before God today. No requests — just reverence.", prayer: "Lord, I want to be a woman who fears You — deeply, lovingly, consistently. Let reverence for You be the foundation of everything I am. Amen."),
